Subject: soc: qcom: llcc-qcom: Reserve ISLAND1 ways on SM8750


The SM8750 table gives the island slice (LLCC_ISLAND1, SCID 12) its way
mask 0x7fffffff as bonus ways and reserves none. Bonus ways are only
allocated when no other slice has reserved them, while reserved ways
belong to the slice alone. The first posting of the SM8750 support had
these ways reserved, as the downstream table shipped for this SoC still
has them (res_ways = 0x7fffffff, no bonus ways). They became bonus ways
when v2 converted the table to designated initializers.

With this table, system suspend resets the SoC once nothing votes for
the LPASS core. On a Xiaomi Pad 8 Pro with LPASS_HW_MACRO_VOTE and
LPASS_HW_DCODEC_VOTE released, all 16 suspend cycles that went to sleep
(15 s2idle, one PSCI system suspend) ended in a reset; the PMIC PON log
shows only PS_HOLD-triggered resets and no PMIC fault. Holding
LPASS_HW_MACRO_VOTE across suspend avoided the reset, but CX then did
not collapse. The reset stayed hidden while the LPASS macro codecs held
both votes from probe, as they did before v7.3.

Reserve the ways again. With that, all six s2idle cycles that went to
sleep (48 to 60 s, no LPASS vote held) resumed normally, with the cxsd
and ddr residencies within 0.1 s of the time asleep. With the votes
released the ADSP enters island at runtime with either table; only
suspend behaves differently. Why the missing reservation ends in a
reset is not visible from Linux.

Fixes: 2c04e58e30ce ("soc: qcom: llcc-qcom: Add support for SM8750")
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20250113-sm8750_llcc_master-v1-3-5389b92e2d7a@quicinc.com
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/llcc-qcom.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/llcc-qcom.c
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/llcc-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/llcc-qcom.c
@@ -3747,7 +3747,7 @@ static const struct llcc_slice_config sm8750_data[] = {
 		.max_cap = 7936,
 		.priority = 7,
 		.fixed_size = true,
-		.bonus_ways = 0x7fffffff,
+		.res_ways = 0x7fffffff,
 	}, {
 		.usecase_id = LLCC_DISP_WB,
 		.slice_id = 23,

